.DS_Store
*.log
*.py[cod]
.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Credentials belong outside the repository. Example files are safe to track.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Agents work in their own worktree under here. They are checkouts, not
# content: a `git add -A` in the main checkout would otherwise commit every
# other agent's working copy into the tree.
.claude/worktrees/

# Local working areas. The README in each explains the rule and is versioned;
# the contents never are.
workbench/*
!workbench/README.md

# Except workbench/active/, which is tracked for alpha. Tyrel's ruling: the live
# drawer is a spot check on what sessions are actually planning, it gets a
# reviewer's eyes on the run plan, and a note a session deletes by mistake is
# recoverable instead of gone. It is cleaned regularly, so it stays small.
#
# The rest of workbench/ stays ignored, and that is the point: archive/, raw/,
# scratch/ and design/ are where the volume lives. The previous repository
# accumulated 320 markdown files until nobody could tell which document was
# true, and tracking the whole drawer is how that happens again.
!workbench/active/
!workbench/active/**
private/*
!private/README.md
scriptorium/*
!scriptorium/README.md

# autoclave/ is deliberately NOT ignored: drafts commit there on work branches
# so the reviewers can read them raw. CI refuses to merge until it is empty,
# which is what keeps main sterile — see autoclave/README.md.
